 "title": "ZnS QDs and S. cerevisiae Interactions and Effects on Microbiota and Mitochondrion",
 "summary": "This cluster revolves around the interactions between ZnS QDs and S. cerevisiae, a yeast organism. S. cerevisiae is correlated with the production of Skatole, an odorous compound, and increases the populations of Lysinibacillus, Proteobacteria, and Sphingobacterium. ZnS QDs cause hypersensitivity in pos5Δ, a gene or protein, and induce the production of ROS, a chemical. They also modulate the function of Mitochondrion and are treated with BY4742, another organism. Additionally, ZnS QDs have higher tolerance in glr1Δ, a gene or protein, and are exposed to wild-type. The presence of ZnS QDs affects the microbiota, including Bacterial ecology, which is affected by odorous compounds.",
